WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.027
In the CASE pivot, each output measure has a different condition.

00:00:04.027 --> 00:00:07.897
The GROUP BY defines one output row per month.

00:00:07.897 --> 00:00:14.167
Inside that month, each SUM looks only at rows belonging to its diagnosis category.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:20.197
This separation between row grain and category condition is the core pivot pattern.

00:00:20.197 --> 00:00:27.897
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:27.897 --> 00:00:31.637
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:31.637 --> 00:00:37.682
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:37.682 --> 00:00:38.400
combination.
